1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,280
Ollie: Good morning, Pip! Race you to the water!

2
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:13,340
Pip: Ollie, the water is gone!

3
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:15,410
Ollie: It was right here yesterday!

4
00:00:16,910 --> 00:00:18,770
Ollie: Why does the water go away?

5
00:00:21,910 --> 00:00:24,540
Ollie: Let's find out!

6
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:59,360
Pip: Maybe the sea is hiding.

7
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:03,940
Ollie: Maybe it went on a trip!

8
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:08,750
Pip: Even the snails are leaving.

9
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:13,950
Gus: I know! The sea ran away. Easy!

10
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:16,370
Ollie: Why would the sea run away?

11
00:01:16,770 --> 00:01:19,270
Gus: Maybe it got bored. Or hungry!

12
00:01:21,150 --> 00:01:24,460
Pip: I don't think seas get hungry.

13
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:32,990
Ollie: The sand is shaped like waves. So the water was here!

14
00:01:34,490 --> 00:01:36,370
Ollie: I'll go find it. Follow me!

15
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:42,240
Pip: Ollie, wait! Bean is still back there!

16
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:47,540
Ollie: Oops. Sorry, Bean. Let's go together.

17
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:52,220
Gus: Ha! I've got a faster way!

18
00:01:52,620 --> 00:01:55,350
Pip: Gus, your faster ways always go wrong.

19
00:01:56,850 --> 00:02:01,690
Gus: Not this time! We bring the sea back ourselves!

20
00:02:03,190 --> 00:02:05,330
Ollie: How, Gus?

21
00:02:05,730 --> 00:02:08,570
Gus: Buckets! Lots and lots of buckets!

22
00:02:15,070 --> 00:02:17,290
Pip: What if we try it the careful way?

23
00:02:17,690 --> 00:02:23,560
Ollie: Let's watch Gus try first. Then we ask Gran Mari.

24
00:02:29,060 --> 00:02:32,240
Gus: See? One bucket, one big splash!

25
00:02:33,740 --> 00:02:36,930
Gus: Hey! Where did it go?

26
00:02:38,430 --> 00:02:40,900
Gus: Whoa, whoa, whoaaa!

27
00:02:48,430 --> 00:02:49,920
Pip: Are you okay, Gus?

28
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:54,160
Gus: I'm fine! I did that on purpose!

29
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:57,960
Ollie: Did you slip, Gus?

30
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:04,010
Gus: No! I was testing the water. It's wet. Very wet.

31
00:03:05,510 --> 00:03:07,660
Ollie: Your bucket water sank into the sand.

32
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:10,440
Gus: It was already wet, so it doesn't count!

33
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:13,410
Pip: Maybe buckets can't bring the sea back.

34
00:03:21,370 --> 00:03:25,920
Ollie: We need help. Let's ask Gran Mari.

35
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:35,810
Gran Mari: Well now, a soggy seagull and a worried otter. What's all this?

36
00:03:37,310 --> 00:03:42,350
Ollie: Gran Mari, why does the water go away?

37
00:03:43,850 --> 00:03:51,960
Gran Mari: Oh, that is a good question, Ollie. Let's find out together.

38
00:03:58,460 --> 00:04:09,030
Gran Mari: This bowl is a pretend ocean. Watch the water, and watch slowly.

39
00:04:10,530 --> 00:04:15,930
Ollie: It moves! High on one side, low on the other!

40
00:04:17,530 --> 00:04:27,140
Gran Mari: See the moon? It pulls on the sea, just a little. Like a very gentle tug.

41
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:33,700
Pip: So the moon makes the water go up and down?

42
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:44,810
Gran Mari: Yes. The water rises up the beach. Then it slides back out. Two times every day.

43
00:04:46,310 --> 00:04:49,880
Ollie: The water didn't run away! It's just out for a while!

44
00:04:58,310 --> 00:05:01,810
Gus: So how long until it comes back?

45
00:05:02,210 --> 00:05:05,810
Gran Mari: Well now, what do you think happens next?

46
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:11,480
Ollie: It slides back to the beach!

47
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:20,760
Gran Mari: The sea keeps its own clock. We can't hurry it. But we can watch it.

48
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:36,860
Ollie: Try it at home! Put water in a bowl. Tilt it very slowly. Watch the water climb one side. Watch it slide away from the other.

49
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:44,530
Ollie: This is our water line. We wait and we watch.

50
00:06:00,030 --> 00:06:04,870
Gus: I can't wait anymore! I'll go get the sea myself!

51
00:06:05,270 --> 00:06:07,300
Bean: Wait!

52
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:14,620
Gus: Okay, okay. I fibbed before. My bucket water didn't count. It all sank away.

53
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:17,180
Gus: I'm sorry I said it was already wet.

54
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:20,940
Ollie: Thanks for telling us the truth, Gus.

55
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:31,760
Pip: It came back all by itself!

56
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:36,700
Ollie: Gran Mari was right! We waited and watched!

57
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:47,960
Ollie: Time for my Wonder Pocket! Three things we learned.

58
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:58,630
Ollie: One. The moon gently pulls on the sea.

59
00:07:00,130 --> 00:07:05,160
Ollie: Two. The water goes up and down two times a day.

60
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:12,830
Ollie: Three. The sea always comes back. We just have to wait.

61
00:07:14,330 --> 00:07:18,610
Ollie: And one kind thing to try today. Wait for a friend.

62
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:25,200
Gus: Bye, everybody! Next time, I'll wait too!
